      "id": "q79nuri",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Matter is anything that possesses mass and occupies physical space.",
        "The primary states of matter are solid, liquid, and gas, each exhibiting distinct physical properties.",
        "Density is defined as mass per unit volume and directly affects buoyancy.",
        "Elasticity is the property of a material to regain its original shape and size after the removal of deforming forces.",
        "Pressure is defined as force applied perpendicular to the surface of an object per unit area."
      ],
      "id": "00rhojo"
